The Problem with tf-idf + Cosine Similarity

library(quanteda)
library(quanteda.textstats)

# Two semantically identical sentences with no shared vocabulary
sentences &lt;- c(
  doc1 = "The borrower defaulted on their loan obligations.",
  doc2 = "The client failed to meet repayment commitments.",
  doc3 = "The borrower defaulted on their loan obligations."  # identical to doc1
)

corp &lt;- corpus(sentences)

sim_tfidf &lt;- corp |&gt;
  tokens(remove_punct = TRUE) |&gt;
  tokens_tolower() |&gt;
  tokens_remove(stopwords("english")) |&gt;
  dfm() |&gt;
  dfm_tfidf() |&gt;
  textstat_simil(method = "cosine", margin = "documents")

as.matrix(sim_tfidf)

     doc1 doc2 doc3
doc1    1    0    1
doc2    0    1    0
doc3    1    0    1


doc1 vs doc3 scores 1.0 (identical). doc1 vs doc2 scores 0, despite being semantically equivalent. This is how far we get with word overlap alone.

